    "ResourceCall": {
      "description": "Calls this run dispatched to one configured external resource.\n\nThis is deliberately identifier-only telemetry. It carries no prompt,\nresult, query text, or token contents. `calls` is incremented on dispatch,\nincluding a request that later fails, because the external service was\nstill asked and may still have billed it.",
      "properties": {
        "calls": {
          "default": 1,
          "title": "Calls",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "id": {
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "enum": [
            "genie-space",
            "vector-index"
          ],
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "tool": {
          "enum": [
            "data_genie",
            "genie_mcp",
            "dictionary_genie",
            "search_semantics"
          ],
          "title": "Tool",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "kind",
        "id",
        "tool",
        "calls"
      ],
      "title": "ResourceCall",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "Source": {
      "description": "One table the run read, and what it read it for.\n\n`role` is the distinction the run already draws internally and used not to\npublish. A table queried for values is `reading`; a table read to look up\nwhat a term means, or to see what columns it has, is `reference`. Both are\nsources of the answer and only the first is a source of its numbers, so a\nflat list presented the dictionary the agent consulted as though the figures\nhad come out of it.\n\nEmpty means unstated, which is what an answer stored before this field\nexisted carries. Readers must say so rather than assuming either role: the\napp has no way to tell from a name, and guessing is how the dictionary came\nto be labelled as the source of the numbers in the first place.",
      "properties": {
        "freshness": {
          "title": "Freshness",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "name": {
          "title": "Name",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "role": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Role",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "name",
        "freshness",
        "role"
      ],
      "title": "Source",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TraceStage": {
      "description": "One step of a run, as the timeline reads it.\n\n`input` and `output` are the allowlisted reader projection. Tool stages keep\ntheir arguments and concrete result, with agent-only retry and safety\nguidance removed. Agent stages keep only a compact task and outcome, never\ntheir model prompt or internal handoff. The size cap lives in `agent.py`.\n\n`depth` and `parent_id` express nesting. A tool-calling loop is a tree, and a\nflat list of siblings misrepresents it as a sequence of equals.",
      "properties": {
        "calls": {
          "default": 1,
          "title": "Calls",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "depth": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Depth",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "duration": {
          "title": "Duration",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "id": {
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "input": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Input",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kind": {
          "title": "Kind",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "name": {
          "title": "Name",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "output": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Output",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "parent_id": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Parent Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "start": {
          "title": "Start",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "status": {
          "enum": [
            "complete",
            "running",
            "partial",
            "failed"
          ],
          "title": "Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "tables": {
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Tables",
          "type": "array"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "name",
        "kind",
        "start",
        "duration",
        "status",
        "calls",
        "input",
        "output",
        "tables",
        "depth",
        "parent_id"
      ],
      "title": "TraceStage",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TraceSummary": {
      "description": "What one run did, as the app reads it back.\n\n`toolCalls` counts EXTERNAL CALLS THE RUN MADE: dictionary Genie, data Genie,\nthe read-only SQL fallback, the synthesis model call, the plotting call. It is\nNOT the number of stages tagged `kind=\"tool\"` and is normally larger, because\n`discover` and `synthesis` are tagged `\"agent\"` and the SQL fallback produces\nno stage of its own.\n\nThe two are different quantities, reported separately: the app exposes the\ntagged stages as `toolStages`. Do not make one derivable from the other.\n\n`prompt_tokens` / `completion_tokens` / `total_tokens` are the sum of every\nchat-completions `usage` block recorded this turn. Zero when the endpoint\ndid not return usage, not when the run made no model calls: the two are not\ndistinguishable from the totals alone, and a missing meter must not look\nlike a free run.\n\n`genie_spaces` are the spaces this run actually called, in the order it first\nreached each, and it is empty for a run that asked Genie nothing. Recorded on\ndispatch rather than on a successful reply, so a run refused by a space it was\nnever shared with still says which space refused it -- which is the run whose\nrouting someone most needs to see.",
      "properties": {
        "completion_tokens": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Completion Tokens",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "genie_spaces": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/GenieSpace"
          },
          "title": "Genie Spaces",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "genie_transport": {
          "default": "direct",
          "enum": [
            "direct",
            "mcp"
          ],
          "title": "Genie Transport",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "id": {
          "title": "Id",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "prompt_tokens": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Prompt Tokens",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "resource_calls": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ResourceCall"
          },
          "title": "Resource Calls",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "stages": {
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/TraceStage"
          },
          "title": "Stages",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "toolCalls": {
          "title": "Toolcalls",
          "type": "integer"
        },
        "totalMs": {
          "title": "Totalms",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "total_tokens": {
          "default": 0,
          "title": "Total Tokens",
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "id",
        "totalMs",
        "toolCalls",
        "stages",
        "genie_spaces",
        "resource_calls",
        "genie_transport",
        "prompt_tokens",
        "completion_tokens",
        "total_tokens"
      ],
      "title": "TraceSummary",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "UnavailableOutput": {
      "description": "A terminal refusal emitted by the served agent inside an HTTP 200.\n\n`code` and `layer` remain open strings on purpose. A newer agent can add a\nterminal code before the app deploys; the app must preserve the refusal and\ndegrade it to its unknown-code fallback rather than misread it as an answer.\nRequest/run ids and execution identity are present on identity refusals and\nabsent on gateway/transport refusals.",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "title": "Code",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "execution_identity": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ExecutionIdentityClaim"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "layer": {
          "title": "Layer",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "message": {
          "title": "Message",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "request_id": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Request Id"
        },
        "retryable": {
          "title": "Retryable",
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        "run_id": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Run Id"
        },
        "type": {
          "const": "unavailable",
          "title": "Type",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "type",
        "code",
        "layer",
        "retryable",
        "message"
      ],
      "title": "UnavailableOutput",
      "type": "object"
    }
